## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design practical multi-tenant localization, content grounding, and integration of Azure services with OpenAI.

## Key Concepts
- Language detection and translation using Azure Text Analytics and Azure Translator
- Grounding OpenAI responses to a KB stored in Azure Blob and indexed by Cognitive Search
- Per-tenant locale settings for currency/date formatting
- Error handling and fallback
- APIM as gateway and request routing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation sketch for data flow
async function handleQuery(input, tenant){
  const lang = detectLang(input);
  const q = translate(input, 'en');
  const grounded = await queryOpenAI(q, tenant);
  const res = translate(grounded, lang, lang);
  return res;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test locale formatting across locales?
- How would you handle translation latency and partial failures?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of Azure OpenAI deployment, API management, knowledge-grounding, data privacy, and governance in a realistic, beginner-friendly setting.

## Key Concepts
- Azure OpenAI Service integration with gateway
- Knowledge-grounding via Azure Cognitive Search
- PII redaction with Text Analytics
- Per-repo policy gating and audit logging to Data Lake

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: redactPII and gate before OpenAI call
function handleRequest(req){
  const redacted = redactPII(req.input);
  if (!policyAllows(req.repo, redacted)) return denyResponse();
  return callOpenAI({input:redacted});
}
```

